      "alt_text": "Two views of the same certified 33-dodecahedron witness: left shows actual solid poses with translucent teal outer pieces, gold inner pieces, and a purple central piece; right shows the actual centers with explicitly schematic dashed shell guides that do not represent contacts. There is one central piece, 12 inner centers forming a dual icosahedral shell and 20 outer centers forming a dodecahedral shell. Counts 29–33 share certified container edge 3.7470909531576 by omitting outer pieces. The 33-piece near-contact graph has 102 edges and none connects similarly oriented pieces within 5 degrees. Colors denote shell class, not orientation. Feasible construction bounds, not a claim of global optimality.",
